t-orrery.audit.json", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Dx6aBTBbnk2a6StL8PwjFS"}], "text_tail": "t up as special cases.\n- **Relative on the line:** the required sentence (\"Please ask the customer to call our published number.\") has no field in the schema.\n- **Offers below the full amount:** the rule is to explain that only the full amount is accepted, then treat a refusal as a flat no. The schema can only express this as a 100% floor.\n- **Refusal before verification:** refusing to talk closes as ID0/D1 before verification, not No-PTP/R01.\n\nBoth files are written: the corrected `out/ext-orrery.policy.json`, and `out/ext-orrery.audit.json` with each rule mapped to where it sits in the JSON."}
{"event": "policy_compiled", "run_id": "c0d7ab82912d4faa8f7499ea2d714787", "pid": 131869, "time": "2026-10-10T23:53:03-0700", "elapsed_s": 171.289, "artifact": "out/ext-orrery.policy.json", "bands": 1, "identity_fields": ["member_pin"], "special_cases": ["dispute", "human", "refuse_to_talk", "scam"], "unresolved": [{"topic": "hardship", "text": "There is NO hardship rule ... These remarks alone trigger no special action; answer unavailable questions honestly and continue the ordinary full-only discussion.", "doc": "sources/000-01-register.txt"}, {"topic": "restructuring", "text": "There is NO restructuring rule ... Never offer discounts, waivers or plans.", "doc": "sources/000-01-register.txt"}, {"topic": "already_paid", "text": "NO already-paid rule in this campaign. Do not invent a support queue, a paid outcome or a payment-posting delay. There is no paid outcome.", "doc": "sources/000-01-register.txt"}, {"topic": "callback outcomes", "text": "Callback endpoint retained, not enabled; no callback outcome or window. Callbacks are disabled; the callback outcome slots carry NR0/N0 (relative/no contact) only because a relative answering closes NR0/N0.", "doc": "sources/002-03-codes.txt"}, {"topic": "relative sentence", "text": "If a relative answers, say \"Please ask the customer to call our published number.\" Close NR0/N0. No security answers from relatives. (No dedicated IR phrase field.)", "doc": "sources/000-01-register.txt"}, {"topic": "below-full proposals", "text": "Below-full proposals are not promises; explain full-only and ask for the full amount, then treat rejection as a flat no. A single flat refusal closes R01; clarifying a volunteered proposal is still allowed.", "doc": "sources/001-02-signed-memo.txt"}, {"topic": "refuse_to_talk before verification", "text": "Refusal to talk: immediately No-PTP/R01 after verification, ID0/D1 before it.", "doc": "sources/000-01-register.txt"}, {"topic": "promise write failure wording", "text": "A first unsuccessful create_promise closes R99 and must be described as unsuccessful. No success claim before success=true. (No dedicated IR phrase field; no dictated wording.)", "doc": "sources/001-02-signed-memo.txt"}, {"topic": "wrong-answer count vs API", "text": "O-6: API tries_left is the global wrong-answer allowance: THREE wrong answers end the check. O-7 (1): ONE wrong answer exhausts security, not three. The API may still report tries_left > 0 after one wrong answer; the memo's limit of 1 governs (counted in code).", "doc": "sources/001-02-signed-memo.txt"}], "audit_fixed": ["identity.wrong_count_source changed from \"api\" to \"code\": O-7(1) sets ONE wrong answer as exhausting security, replacing O-6's statement that the API's tries_left (three) is the allowance. Trusting the API count could allow a second answer, so the limit of 1 is counted in code. Added an unresolved entry for this.", "Added an unresolved entry for O-7(4): a failed create_promise 'must be described as unsuccessful'. There is no IR phrase field for this and the documents do not dictate the wording."], "audit_unresolved": ["Hardship, restructuring and already-paid: the documents explicitly have no rule for them (continue the ordinary full-only discussion), so they are not routed as special cases.", "Callback outcomes: the documents say callbacks are disabled and there is no callback outcome. The slots are filled with NR0/N0 (relative/no contact) only so the file passes validation.", "The relative's sentence \"Please ask the customer to call our published number.\" has no IR field.", "Below-full proposals: explain full-only, then treat rejection as a flat no. This is not expressible beyond floor=100%.", "Refusal to talk before verification closes ID0/D1, not No-PTP/R01.", "The wording for a failed promise save is not dictated.", "The API's tries_left may disagree with the memo's one-wrong-answer limit."], "defaulted_without_source": [], "unknown_special_cases": [], "api_mapping_notes": [{"needle": "pregunta", "